    "synthetic": true,
    "notes": "SYNTHETIC. The state in which `crewReckoning.ts` is prepared to say how well it knows a number. Jebediah's radiation and stress accumulators are both observed CLIMBING across three unevenly spaced samples, which is what gives the fit a residual and therefore a standard error; Bob's one rule is flat, which is positive evidence that its input resource is still aboard, so his meter carries no marks at all and the two states can be read side by side in one picture. The two bands on Jeb are deliberately different widths, and each is drawn as a fraction of its own rule's fatal threshold: the radiation interval is about 1.7 of 50 units, a visible gap on the track, while the stress interval is about 0.003 of 1 and its two marks sit close enough to read as one. The samples' x-axis is each entry's own `asOfUt`, never the wire time, so every sample states both."
  },
